{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses","id":946107,"title":"Begotten and Hopeful: What do Beasts think of Princesses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T06:05:30-07:00","id":946107,"title":"Begotten and Hopeful: What do Beasts think of Princesses?","content":"Over on the Princess forums we're discussed what Princesses think of Beasts a few times (Princess is &quot;a storytelling game of fighting fear&quot;, the conclusion is obvious) but I'm feeling aimlessly curious about the other side of that equation. What do Beasts think about Princesses?<br /> <br /> I thought I would ask the experts here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:25:34-07:00","id":946147,"title":"","content":"If I were going to do a Princess/Beast game, Princesses would be &quot;heroes gone right,&quot; the beast's mirror opposites and twin siblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:00:58-07:00","id":946340,"title":"","content":"I personally like to imagine it's an uneasy relationship, but that there is a relationship all the same-Beasts can still count the Nobles as family, and might see them as the better half of Heroes, while the Princesses feel ill at-ease but easily see where the expectations fall.<br /> <br /> They each have seen far worse, and while their relationship speak to antithesis, those darker spheres reveal the place for the other. Uncomfortable, but workable-and isn't that the way with family and hope?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:07:22-07:00","id":946347,"title":"","content":"Really it depends on the Beast, I'd imagine. As StSword said, I can imagine that Begotten Ocultists might attempt to argue that the Hopeful are the Children's equals and opposites, born from the Bright Dream, possibly attempting to make parallels between the Tranformed State and a Begotten who's called down their Lair or merged with their Horror. One emotion that might come up among the Children is jealousy. After all, they're forced to hurt people to feed their Hunger; sure, they use the framework of lessons to try to lessen the impact, but in the end they either hurt people consciously or they let themselves grow Starving and hurt people anyway. The Nobility instead &quot;Feed&quot; through heroism and making the world a better place, by making people happier and safer. Why? Why should they get to have it so easy? I mean, the Radiant do not have it easy in the slightest, but we're talking perception, not facts. At the same time, the Princesses can be a source of hope to the Children. After all, Family Dinner allows one to Feed through facilitating the feeding of Kin, and the Nobility, again, feed by making the world a better place. A Beast at odd with their nature might be able to find a way out... provided the Noble they approach doesn't mistake them for a Darkspawn and try to execute or &quot;fix&quot; them. <br /> <br /> Speaking of Kinship, one aspect that will influence the question is your thoughts therein. Is the idea of them being Kin disgust you, do you have some special idea for it, what?<br /> <br /> And finally, I imagine you could easily draw some parallels between Mirrors and Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:37:29-07:00","id":946377,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946340#post946340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but workable-and isn't that the way with family and hope?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for anyone else, but there's very little &quot;dark&quot; in my familal relationships.<br /> <br /> Lucky me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> [edit] Wait, Did I just answer a rhetorical question? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946347#post946347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or &quot;fix&quot; them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You read Ride to Damascus?<br /> <br /> They were origonally an idea I had for Princesses, and the Embassy to Stories can Talecraft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946347#post946347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Kinship, one aspect that will influence the question is your thoughts therein. Is the idea of them being Kin disgust you, do you have some special idea for it, what?</div> </div> </div> </div> Disgust? No. I feel Kinship gives a little too much mechanical support to the Begotten's theory that all monsters are related, but... Why on Earth would I be disgusted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946347#post946347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, I imagine you could easily draw some parallels between Mirrors and Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well obviously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-08-2016, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:40:34-07:00","id":946420,"title":"","content":"I was interested in this idea as well and spun it as Beast and Princesses are usually at ends with each other over their mirrored nature. Though do find similar goals between their enemies and there is no doubt a strong Hero may have attempted to Kidnap and take his 'blessing' from a Princess by force. A Beast might come into conflict with the nightmare creatures the Hopeful fight, there is nothing wrong with fear if you learn from it but there is a status quo. They may find kinship with each other, some of their abilities parallel.<br /> <br /> Would a Hero appear to have no Hope of coming back or are they more of a living nightmare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:00:36-07:00","id":946434,"title":"","content":"I'd think Storms, at least, would slot them into the &quot;BURN IT&quot; category. Princesses fight fear, and Beasts basically <i>are</i> fear-given-form. At least enough for Storms to say &quot;too much like a Darkspawn to take chances&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:11:02-07:00","id":946498,"title":"","content":"Question, which category has the title &quot;Princess?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T23:00:11-07:00","id":946762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946498#post946498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, which category has the title &quot;Princess?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Princess: the Hopeful. It's a fangame, click my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T00:57:54-07:00","id":946798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946762#post946762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Princess: the Hopeful. It's a fangame, click my sig.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, when you mentioned forum and with all the different sobriquets different splats have I couldn't be sure if that wasn't a title attached to a different splat on the Onyx Path forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:24:27-07:00","id":947225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=946434#post946434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think Storms, at least, would slot them into the &quot;BURN IT&quot; category. Princesses fight fear, and Beasts basically <i>are</i> fear-given-form. At least enough for Storms to say &quot;too much like a Darkspawn to take chances&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or worse yet, they might decide that Beasts are enough of a lesser evil for a temporary alliance, before turning on them and brutally murdering them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:01:38-07:00","id":982616,"title":"","content":"It could depend on the way the story is told. With Beasts and Princesses there is an increased chance that the Hero antagonist will try to come and save the day. Depending on the &quot;heroes&quot; actions the Princess might view him as an utter brute and instead encourage the Beast to slay the hero (which would be kind of entertaining to watch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:39:58-07:00","id":983403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=982616#post982616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Princess might view him as an utter brute and instead encourage the Beast to slay the hero (which would be kind of entertaining to watch).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have to be a pretty low Belief Princess to choose murder over incarcaration or hospitalisation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:57:42-07:00","id":983409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=983403#post983403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would have to be a pretty low Belief Princess to choose murder over incarcaration or hospitalisation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That runs into the problem of whether Heroes can be cured, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:33:23-07:00","id":983425,"title":"","content":"Still. They can certainly be jailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:48:56-07:00","id":983440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=983409#post983409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That runs into the problem of whether Heroes can be cured, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be, sort of. You just have to convince them that there's more to life than being a slayer of monsters. The book mentions that sometimes they even figure this out on their own and just kind of stop for seemingly no reason. They're still Heroes but they no longer feel that endless desire to slay the Beast. They may even end up channeling that drive into more healthy activities that benefit their communities as some of the higher integrity Heroes do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:27:34-07:00","id":984201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=983440#post983440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be, sort of. You just have to convince them that there's more to life than being a slayer of monsters. The book mentions that sometimes they even figure this out on their own and just kind of stop for seemingly no reason. They're still Heroes but they no longer feel that endless desire to slay the Beast. They may even end up channeling that drive into more healthy activities that benefit their communities as some of the higher integrity Heroes do.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/Main/DefeatMeansFriendship\" target=\"_blank\">Defeat Means Friendship</a> crops up in plenty of Magical Girl anime. Seems to fit thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:41:13-07:00","id":985155,"title":"","content":"Beast sees Princess, and thinks 'yummy.'<br /> <br /> The context of this depends on the Hunger involved, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:09:36-07:00","id":985207,"title":"","content":"This determination to see the canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them and the non-canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them as virulently opposed to each other hurts my brain a bit.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, it would not be an easy relationship, but I think the contention would only be slightly higher than with, say, a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:42:09-07:00","id":985221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985207#post985207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This determination to see the canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them and the non-canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them as virulently opposed to each other hurts my brain a bit.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, it would not be an easy relationship, but I think the contention would only be slightly higher than with, say, a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see them as virulently opposed <i>overall</i>, but they connect to other supernaturals in <i>wildly different ways.</i><br /> <br /> Beasts are everybody's cousin, and they encourage them to let their freak flags fly. Nobility are everybody's friend, and encourage them to resist their darker impulses.<br /> <br /> I don't think Beasts and Princesses are completely unable to get along, but I think there's a lot of issues they need to get around. It certainly would be easier in the case of Begotten who work constructively, though. A good Beast's influence could be very liberating to Nobility, and the right Princess could help keep the Begotten's appetites focused on something positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:48:53-07:00","id":985222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985221#post985221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see them as virulently opposed <i>overall</i>, but they connect to other supernaturals in <i>wildly different ways.</i><br /> <br /> Beasts are everybody's cousin, and they encourage them to let their freak flags fly. Nobility are everybody's friend, and encourage them to resist their darker impulses.<br /> <br /> I don't think Beasts and Princesses are completely unable to get along, but I think there's a lot of issues they need to get around. It certainly would be easier in the case of Begotten who work constructively, though. A good Beast's influence could be very liberating to Nobility, and the right Princess could help keep the Begotten's appetites focused on something positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Even with the Wildly Different Ways, at the end of the day, it's not always set to be &quot;RARGH, RARGH&quot;, even if there is a hell of an initial barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:13:14-07:00","id":985237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985207#post985207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This determination to see the canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them and the non-canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them as virulently opposed to each other hurts my brain a bit.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, it would not be an easy relationship, but I think the contention would only be slightly higher than with, say, a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's in the subtitle, Arc.<br /> <br /> Princess is a game about Fighting Fear.<br /> <br /> Beasts need to cause fear to eat for another day.<br /> <br /> It kind of gets them off on the wrong foot by default.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's not to say they always hate each other-Beasts aren't the kind of creatures to dislike Princesses by any stretch of the imagination. It's just tense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T20:44:22-07:00","id":985250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985237#post985237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the subtitle, Arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The subtitle that in practice means &quot;give people hope and clean up the festering pits of despair,&quot; yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts need to cause fear to eat for another day. </div> </div> </div>They need to ensure somebody misses a step or loses their phone or gashes their hand. Dropping into the primeval flight-reflex for a moment is not the pervasive awfulness of a Taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-11-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T21:07:52-07:00","id":985257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985250#post985250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need to ensure somebody misses a step or loses their phone or gashes their hand. Dropping into the primeval flight-reflex for a moment is not the pervasion awfulness of a Taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was. What I meant to say is that Beasts, from a cursory glance, look like exactly the kind of people who don't <i>need </i>the Dark to be pretty awful-hell, Princesses even cross wits with a variety of dreamborn monster of their own fairly regularly. Many, perhaps most, aren't-and in fact I'd dare say Begotten happily try to purify the Dark on their own, since it isn't something you want in your backyard. But some Begotten, perhaps many, don't actually care about the request the Dark Mother makes of them to turn their Hungers to good ends. Those Beasts are probably known to <i>cause </i>Dark infestations by their crueler feasts.<br /> <br /> That's going to leave a pretty long memory in the Nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:02:28-07:00","id":985311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985250#post985250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subtitle that in practice means &quot;give people hope</div> </div> </div> </div> What is hope if not the possibility that tomorrow is better than today?<br /> <br /> What is a better tomorrow if not one that is one step further from mankind's savage and primordial past?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Courts of Hearts and Diamonds would agree with the implied answer to that rhetorical question. Spades would neither agree nor disagree since they don't think in these sorts of terms. Swords would deny that there is such thing as an &quot;inner ape&quot;, they think there is an inner angel instead. Clubs would disagree with the idea of abandoning the &quot;inner ape&quot; and instead they'd wish to befriend it. (Though friends don't trigger the flight or fight response).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985250#post985250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need to ensure somebody misses a step or loses their phone or gashes their hand. Dropping into the primeval flight-reflex for a moment is not the pervasive awfulness of a Taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the fact that I cannot see a charachter who's actions are on the level of Bart Simpson as a viable monster in a horror story. There's three different Invocations that would be strongly opposed to a beast &quot;just making you stumble&quot;.<br /> <br /> Terra believes in society and social contracts. And there are a <i>lot</i> of highly regarded social contracts regarding education and therapy. You might call it &quot;just a gash&quot; but corporal punishment has been considered unacceptable behaviour for teachers for years. To a follower of Terra it's not &quot;just a gash&quot;, it's defiling something sacred. (Of course, nothing actually stops a Beast getting qualifications and rigorously following all the professional ethics guidelines but I imagine it's fairly rare.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Acqua isn't entirely focused around education, but it does hold education to be one of the fundamental forces of good and claims all Princesses have a duty to educate themselves and others. Princesses who believe in Acqua who see a Beast's lessons would consider the quality of those lessons to be of paramount impotence. Imagine someone with the equivalent of PhDs in educational theory, psychology and developmental psychology (if an Acqua Princess doesn't have superhuman intelligence she'll know people who does) reviewing a Beast's intended lesson and their method to teach it. If a Beast insists on tasty lessons over good lessons, or worse, is teaching lessons the Princess considers wrong that's a huge deal to believers in Acqua. And most practitioners of Acqua would consider teaching people to use the fight or flight reflex (as opposed to calm rational thought) to be wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> To Fuoco if something hurts someone, it is wrong. Even if it's just a gash in the hand, the wilful attempt to harm someone goes against everything Fuoco believes in. Even if it's not serious enough for the Princess to think she needs to intervene it will still affect her view of the Beast. Believers in Fuoco would also be extreemly suspicious of anyone claiming they don't have a choice other than to harm others and assume it's either immorality or ignorance rather than a genuine lack of options. (and thanks to family dinner Beasts have plenty of options). <hr /><br /> Basically your interpretation of the subtitle is a vast oversimplification. Saying Princesses give people hope and clean up festering pits of despair is like saying vampires drink blood. Yes they do. But nobody plays Vampire as nothing but back to back feeding scenes.<br /> <br /> You cannot talk about Princess without pointing out that their morality trait is Belief. Every psychologically healthy Princess has deeply held moral convictions and principals. If you want to examine Princesses views on the Begotten, you have to look at those Philosophies and what they say about Beasts and Beasts' own philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> You can't just point out that the Darkness is worse and leave it at that. It doesn't need to be as bad as the Darkness for Princesses to care. There is an entire Z-Splat of Princesses who specialise in <u>white collar crime</u>.<br /> <br /> <br /> And obviously Princesses aren't going to attack anyone they have a philosophical disagreement with on sight. Left and right wing princesses can be friends and two different followers of Acqua can teach contradictory lessons about the unsettled questions of the day without loosing respect for each other so long as they're honest about what's known and what's speculative.<br /> <br /> What I am objecting to is the idea that Princesses would write of &quot;just as gash&quot; as no big deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> (The Invocations are far from the whole story about Princess' beliefs, but when generalising about the entire splat - they're close enough.)<br /> <br /> (Fun fact. The Princesses who specialise in white collar crime came from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8l1PMVvfjDM\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985257#post985257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd dare say Begotten happily try to purify the Dark on their own, since it isn't something you want in your backyard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't the Begotten consider Dark Creatures to be Kin? I thought the Begotten considered everything to be kin. They even have Hunger as common ground.<br /> <br /> Also don't Begotten have a special rule that makes it safer to explore other realms? E.G. they resist the thorns like Changelings? If so they'd actually gain bonus from being within Taint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985250#post985250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The