lean up festering pits of despair is like saying vampires drink blood. Yes they do. But nobody plays Vampire as nothing but back to back feeding scenes.<br /> <br /> You cannot talk about Princess without pointing out that their morality trait is Belief. Every psychologically healthy Princess has deeply held moral convictions and principals. If you want to examine Princesses views on the Begotten, you have to look at those Philosophies and what they say about Beasts and Beasts' own philosophical convictions.<br /> <br /> You can't just point out that the Darkness is worse and leave it at that. It doesn't need to be as bad as the Darkness for Princesses to care. There is an entire Z-Splat of Princesses who specialise in white collar crime.<br /> <br /> <br /> And obviously Princesses aren't going to attack anyone they have a philosophical disagreement with on sight. Left and right wing princesses can be friends and two different followers of Acqua can teach contradictory lessons about the unsettled questions of the day without loosing respect for each other so long as they're honest about what's known and what's speculative.<br /> <br /> What I am objecting to is the idea that Princesses would write of &quot;just as gash&quot; as no big deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> (The Invocations are far from the whole story about Princess' beliefs, but when generalising about the entire splat - they're close enough.)<br /> <br /> (Fun fact. The Princesses who specialise in white collar crime came from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8l1PMVvfjDM\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985257#post985257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd dare say Begotten happily try to purify the Dark on their own, since it isn't something you want in your backyard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't the Begotten consider Dark Creatures to be Kin? I thought the Begotten considered everything to be kin. They even have Hunger as common ground.<br /> <br /> Also don't Begotten have a special rule that makes it safer to explore other realms? E.G. they resist the thorns like Changelings? If so they'd actually gain bonus from being within Taint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985207#post985207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This determination to see the canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them and the non-canon splat most inclined to reaching out to other supernaturals and connecting with them as virulently opposed to each other hurts my brain a bit.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, it would not be an easy relationship, but I think the contention would only be slightly higher than with, say, a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what malonkey1 said. I think a lot of that disagreement comes down to unstated assumptions.<br /> <br /> If you imagine that the hypothetical average Beast is a serial killer or engages in sustained and targeted psychological abuse in order to feed then you'll assume, quite justifiably, that the hypothetical average beast is someone a Princess will go out of her way to stop before they can hurt anyone else; and if the only way to stop him is violence then it's justified.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you assume that the hypothetical average Beast &quot;ensures somebody misses a step or loses their phone or gashes their hand&quot; then you might think a Princess' distaste for the Beast's feeding will be outweighed by her innate empathy or the practical benefits of an alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record I'm somewhere in the middle but closer to the latter. Stealing your phone just isn't a viable source of horror IMO. (I have on occasion misplaced my phone. It was shocking, it was not horrific and did not teach me any lessons).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-11-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T07:11:07-07:00","id":985393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985311#post985311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you imagine that the hypothetical average Beast is a serial killer or engages in sustained and targeted psychological abuse in order to feed then you'll assume, quite justifiably, that the hypothetical average beast is someone a Princess will go out of her way to stop before they can hurt anyone else; and if the only way to stop him is violence then it's justified.<br /> these<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you assume that the hypothetical average Beast &quot;ensures somebody misses a step or loses their phone or gashes their hand&quot; then you might think a Princess' distaste for the Beast's feeding will be outweighed by her innate empathy or the practical benefits of an alliance.<br /> <br /> For the record I'm somewhere in the middle but closer to the latter. Stealing your phone just isn't a viable source of horror IMO. (I have on occasion misplaced my phone. It was shocking, it was not horrific and did not teach me any lessons).</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to me is that it's not just stealing your phone. There's a story in Page 62 of the core rulebook where the Beast starts by trying to steal someone's watch and ends by killing them. To me part of the horror isn't just that Horror drives the Beast to do these petty acts (although there is some horror in that the Beast is driven to do these things to sate their Horror) but that you can't tell a Beast with Low Satiety, &quot;Help me against the bad guy and feed your Horror&quot; if you're not ready for them to possibly go from zero to murder in six seconds.<br /> <br /> I've been interested for a while how Princesses and Beasts have these weird connections to each other (Connections to dreams, connections to human emotions, the dual identity aspects, claims to seek to instill virtues in humanity) etc. But I personally think the two are almost incompatible with each other. Short-term, their first interaction would most likely be the Princess finding the Beast in the middle of feeding, which would very likely lead to conflict. Long-term, I'm having trouble seeing many relationships besides &quot;Beast sees Princess as Kin in principle but in practice is resentful at the Princess's attempts to restrain them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know I speak from reading and not experience, but I'm realizing that playing the Beast around other supernaturals can very easily become an analogy to playing the Shadow from Wraith: the Oblivion, and from what I read, that was very hard to play well.<br /> <br /> Please correct me if I am wrong on any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:58:26-07:00","id":985655,"title":"","content":"I said 'yummy' mainly as a joke, btw. In case that wasn't clear. Because they're <i>Princesses</i>, get it? Kidnap her and take her to your Lair!<br /> <br /> I'll be in my corner, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:02:57-07:00","id":985791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=983425#post983425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still. They can certainly be jailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that is a fair point. It might also be possible for the Beast to imprison the hero, but I have to do more reading to be sure.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This is a bit off-topic but I am curious about this princess thing you are talking about in the OP. Does it have anything to do with the link in your sig?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:53:15-07:00","id":985819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985791#post985791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that is a fair point. It might also be possible for the Beast to imprison the hero, but I have to do more reading to be sure.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This is a bit off-topic but I am curious about this princess thing you are talking about in the OP. Does it have anything to do with the link in your sig?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a> is a real good fangame that places Magical Girls (and Guys) in the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:20:28-07:00","id":985962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985819#post985819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a> is a real good fangame that places Magical Girls (and Guys) in the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed interesting. Personally I am not a fan of magical girls (I don't hate them their just kind of... meh to me) but the idea of a character taking on the role of a princess in a Beast campaign does sound interesting.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> As how the beast might act toward a princess it could depend on the beast's hunger. For example a beast whose hunger is punishment might capture a princess if she did something wrong. On the other hand a beast whose hunger is hoarding could capture princess in order to feed its hunger. Or perhaps the princess is taken as a sort of hostage in order for the beast to negotiate in order to satisfy some other form of hunger.<br /> <br /> &quot;Allow me to destroy a potion of the city and I will return my hostage.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is also a chance that the beast could gain special abilities from the princess, similar to how beasts gain powers from other monsters they have gathered as allies (vampires, werewolves, changelings, etc...). Such a situation could actually be beneficial to both the beast and the princess (especially if she wants a powerful, supernatural body guard).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:52:18-07:00","id":986073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/946107-begotten-and-hopeful-what-do-beasts-think-of-princesses?p=985962#post985962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand a beast whose hunger is hoarding could capture princess in order to feed its hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Cough</i>Harem<i>Cough</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:38:33-07:00","id":986123,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can't see many Princess/Beast pairings that make sense. I see Princesses more likely to engage in a tug of war with a Beast rather than get along. Beasts encourage vampires to hunt outside the safety and consent of a willing herd, they encourage werewolves to eat more people and spirits, they encourage mages to slip closer to low Wisdom and so on. In general, Beasts are naturally inclined towards enabling destructive influences. Meanwhile, a Princess would want that vampire, mage, werewolf etc to push towards high / balanced Integrity equivalents. Its like watching a friend fall under the bad habits of a destructive relationship. <br /> <br /> Granted, this is just a gross over-generalization, and individuals matter. But I honestly think that, in this case, the similarities that Princesses and Beasts have would push them more towards conflict than friendship. They both want the same resource (friendship with other supernaturals), but the nature of that friendship really can't be shared. They want to go in two mutually exclusive directions.<br /> <br /> And then, lets look at the case of Princess and Beast without any Kin. Just the two of them alone in Detroit and no other supernaturals around for some reason or another. The Beast and Princess become Kin. Now, the Beast is either going to need to go out and hurt people somehow in order to feed him/her/zeself or rely on Family Dinner. Given the natural sadistic nature of the Begotten, and the fact that harming others is a <i>breaking point</i> for a Princess, we've already got issues. I don't think that Call of Duty or Circle qualifies as a &quot;genuine&quot; hunt, so I'm going to argue that Family Dinner doesn't apply*. Beasts instinctually want to grow their Lair, which is done through Integrity (and equivalent) losses; causing others to lose Integirty means our Princess suffers breaking points again. Meanwhile, the Princess's friends are important to her; that said, Circle only applies to mortal friends, and specifically excludes supernatural friends. <br /> <br /> All in all, the Princess and Beast are supernaturally incompatable. I don't see anything that would really suggest they'd get along like a Princess or Beast would naturally want to get along with other supernaturals. Now, individuals can be friends, and likely have fun with any number of things unrelated to supernatural nature. You don't need to have supernatural backing to call someone a friend or family member. But the lack of affirmation from dealing with a Beast as a friend, or a Princess as a family member, can undermine a lot of the assumed relationship. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}